§§ `9.4 Grace period and lapse`

-- First policy year: a regular basic premium not paid before its due date has 60 days of
-- grace; still unpaid after them, the contract lapses, and the Policyholder receives the
-- surrender value on the next Valuation Date after the lapse date. 9.1 says "on or before"
-- the due date and 9.4 "before" it; a payment ON the due date is on time (NOTES.md fork
-- register). The grace period's last day is the 60th day after the due date; the lapse
-- date is the day after that.
-- src:351 | Gia hạn đóng phí bảo hiểm và Mất hiệu lực Hợp
-- src:352 | đồng
-- src:353 | Trong năm đầu tiên của Hợp đồng, nếu phí bảo hiểm cơ
-- src:354 | bản định kỳ không được thanh toán trước ngày đến hạn
-- src:358 | đóng phí, hợp đồng được áp dụng 60 ngày gia hạn. Hợp
-- src:359 | đồng sẽ mất hiệu lực nếu phí bảo hiểm vẫn không được
-- src:360 | thanh toán sau thời gian gia hạn nêu trên. Bên mua bảo
-- src:361 | hiểm được nhận lại giá trị hoàn lại của Hợp Đồng, giá
-- src:362 | được xác định vào ngày định giá kế tiếp sau ngày Hợp
-- src:363 | đồng bảo hiểm bị xem là mất hiệu lực.
@ref Article 9.4, first paragraph (src 353-358)
GIVEN `the due date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the grace period of a premium due on` `the due date` MEANS
    `the due date` PLUS 60

@ref Article 9.4, first paragraph (src 358-360)
GIVEN `the due date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day after the grace period of a premium due on` `the due date` MEANS
    `the due date` PLUS 61

@ref Article 9.4, first and second paragraphs (src 353-367)
GIVEN `the premium`        IS A `A regular premium falling due`
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The outcome of a regular premium falling due`
`Article 9.4 — what follows from` `the premium` `, for a contract effective on` `the effective date` MEANS
    IF   `the policy year in which` (`the premium`'s `due date`) `falls, for a contract effective on` `the effective date` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `no grace period, the premium falling due after the first policy year`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the premium`'s `date paid`
         WHEN JUST d  THEN BRANCH
                             IF d AT MOST `the premium`'s `due date` THEN `paid on or before the due date`
                             IF d AT MOST `the last day of the grace period of a premium due on` (`the premium`'s `due date`)
                                                                     THEN `paid within the grace period`
                             OTHERWISE `the contract lapses on` (`the day after the grace period of a premium due on` (`the premium`'s `due date`))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the contract lapses on` (`the day after the grace period of a premium due on` (`the premium`'s `due date`))

@ref Article 9.4, first paragraph (src 360-363)
GIVEN `the lapse date`  IS A DATE
      `the valuations`  IS A LIST OF `A valuation of the account`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 9.4 — the surrender value paid on a first-year lapse on` `the lapse date` `, among` `the valuations` MEANS
    `the surrender value on the next Valuation Date after` `the lapse date` `among` `the valuations`

-- The same first-year rule as a duty with its consequence: the Policyholder must pay within
-- the 60 days (the clock is in days, day 0 the due date); if not, the contract lapses and
-- the Company must pay the surrender value. The text gives the Company no time to pay it,
-- so that duty carries no WITHIN.
@ref Article 9.4, first paragraph (src 353-363)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act`
`Article 9.4 — the first-year premium and its grace period` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Policyholder`
    MUST   `pay the regular basic premium`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   ( PARTY `the Company`
             MUST  `pay the surrender value`
             HENCE FULFILLED )

-- From the second policy year: the grace period counts from the day the surrender value is
-- found not enough to meet the monthly risk premium and policy fee.
